  "modeling_notes": [
    "The ordinary Standard Track is modeled. Computer Engineering, IA, Cybersecurity, Software Engineering, DNIMAS, and accelerated pathways are excluded.",
    "Norfolk State publishes the Standard Track course table under the heading Curriculum and makes it the only course-level statement of the degree. Although CourseLeaf's generic table class renders the words Plan of Study Grid, the page does not call it sample, suggested, recommended, or illustrative; the four table totals close exactly to 120. The composition therefore treats the rows as the required curriculum while discarding their year-by-year sequencing.",
    "The published summary is 40 General Education + 53 Core Major + 27 Requirements Electives + 0 Other = 120. The same 120 credits are organized here by requirement semantics because the curriculum does not label each row with one of those four accounting buckets.",
    "The fixed named computing, mathematics, and technical-writing rows total 64; two laboratory-science selections total eight; the remaining explicit General Education rows total 27; upper-level CS/Math choices total 18; and free elective capacity is three.",
    "The 40-credit General Education Core includes Digital/Computer, Mathematics, and Natural Sciences categories that are supplied inside the fixed computing/math/science curriculum. Zero-increment gates retain those category requirements without counting the same credits twice.",
    "The curriculum displays 18 upper-level CS-or-Math elective credits while the adjacent Major Electives authority requires at least 15 credits from its enumerated CSC menu. The model therefore requires five menu courses plus one additional CSC-menu or 300-level MATH course."
  ],
